  "body": "Follow-up to #128 (first slice: `camcraft-cli mcp`, branch issue/128-mcp-server).\n\nToday `add_operation` takes `source: \"stock\"` or a model name only. An agent cannot pick the faces, edge chains or loops an operation machines (`SrcRef::Selection`, `SetOperationGeometry`), nor the area controls.\n\nWanted: a tool that lists a model's features with stable ids (the geometry-hash ids `model::features_of` exposes), and a tool that sets an op's selection through `SetOperationGeometry`, so the change is undoable. Also the area controls through `EditOperationParams::with_area`.\n\nDone means: an MCP test picks a pocket's floor loop off an imported STL, generates and verifies, and `undo` restores the previous source.\n",
